What this package contributes: the three re-annealed query modules of the
source-assisted complex word (modules/: pair module n = 10, all-but-one
module n = 9, disjoint-triple module p = 11, found by simulated annealing
from PR168 v4's modules against the exact compile ledger of the aligned
word), one frozen compilation recipe applied to them and, as the control, to
PR168 v4's own modules (layers/), aligned_word.py (PR194's source-aligned
word with the module files and a frozen physical layer as inputs),
paircheck.py (an independent re-check of the reuse pairs with five mutation
controls), normalize_scatter.py (the star scatter by re-signing the
registers of retained totals with unit -1), the discovery driver
discovery/make_layer.py, and the four resulting programs with their checks.
